  "notes": [
    "All five final scenarios passed. Each transport completed 20000 measured calls and 1000 additional mutation-verification calls; every operation p99 is at most 50 ms.",
    "Collection was sequential and isolated from compiler and test jobs. No frequency pinning was applied; bursts have a 400 ms launch cutoff, a 500 ms/1000-call hard limit and at least 250 ms cooldown. Each scenario has a 90-second deadline.",
    "Ordinary transport scenarios run origin, engine and client in separate native processes, with one fixture task maintaining 1000 active ranges. Eight actual mutation types use a separate auxiliary task.",
    "List calls project 128 rows; file and URI calls project 32 sources of about 2 KiB each. firstResponseBytes records the first response for each operation.",
    "Measured stdio uses OS pipes; its stalled second writer uses a loopback socket. Stalled events use 512 KiB coalesced fixture notifications through the production WebSocket broker.",
    "Memory values are sampled maxima; hard RPC and resident limits are enforced by permits. Windows RSS reports working set. Control metrics span the engine runtime and are not latency percentiles.",
    "The approximately 1 ms owner budget is cooperative. The largest observed transport owner turn was 1.815 ms; the maximum step count was 12, below the limit of 32.",
    "Administrative measurements use the production in-process backend with zero active ranges. Urgent probes follow observed bulk progress. Import/export/save/purge cardinalities and separate shutdown durations are reported.",
    "Transport shutdownDrainUs ends at engine process exit; fixtureCleanupUs measures origin cleanup separately. Administrative shutdownDrainUs includes owner/session shutdown in process.",
    "supersededRuns retains the preliminary HTTP failure and administrative result from the earlier binary. They are excluded from final acceptance. The HTTP failure prompted productive-turn yielding; no latency, burst or scenario gate was relaxed.",
    "Native Linux acceptance remains explicitly deferred until CI is ready. The historical September 13 status/global-template report does not validate this implementation.",
    "The sourceCommit and original artifact hashes identify the pre-publication history. publishedSourceCommit identifies the corresponding sanitized implementation; benchmark measurements are unchanged."
  ],
